  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of sustainable development has been widely discussed in recent years. It refers to the ability of a country or community to meet its current needs without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs. This idea is not new, but it has gained significant attention due to the growing awareness of environmental issues such as climate change and pollution.\n\nIn order to achieve sustainable development, governments, businesses, and individuals must work together to reduce waste, increase energy efficiency, and promote renewable energy sources. For example, some countries have implemented policies to encourage the use of electric vehicles, while others have invested in large-scale solar panel installations.\n\nHowever, despite these efforts, many experts argue that sustainable development is still a distant goal. They point out that the current pace of consumption and production is unsustainable and will eventually lead to catastrophic consequences. Therefore, it is essential for individuals, governments, and businesses to take immediate action to reduce their ecological footprint and promote sustainable practices.\n\nIn conclusion, sustainable development is not just an idealistic concept, but a necessary step towards ensuring the well-being of future generations. It requires a fundamental shift in our values and behaviors, as well as significant investments in new technologies and infrastructure.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What does the term 'sustainable development' refer to?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The ability of a country or community to meet its current needs\", \"A concept that focuses on reducing waste and pollution\", \"An idea that prioritizes economic growth over environmental concerns\", \"A theory that aims to balance human needs with environmental protection\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The ability of a country or community to meet its current needs without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the text, what is one way that countries can promote sustainable development?\",\n      \"options\": [\"By investing in large-scale solar panel installations\", \"By encouraging the use of electric vehicles\", \"By reducing waste and increasing energy efficiency\", \"All of the above\"],\n      \"answer\": \"By reducing waste and increasing energy efficiency\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards sustainable development?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Cautious optimism\", \"Pessimism\", \"Neutrality\", \"Skepticism\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Optimism\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"According to the text, what is a potential consequence of not adopting sustainable practices?\",\n      \"options\": [\"A slight increase in energy costs\", \"A moderate decrease in economic growth\", \"Catastrophic consequences for the environment and human well-being\", \"No significant impact on the planet\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Catastrophic consequences for the environment and human well-being\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the text?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The importance of reducing waste and pollution\", \"The benefits of investing in renewable energy sources\", \"The need for sustainable development to ensure a better future\", \"The challenges of implementing sustainable practices\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The need for sustainable development to ensure a better future\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
